From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-controller 99997: a leg has no struct sta, so stop requiring one

handle_sta_link_metrics_response() starts by resolving the reported address in
sta_table and returns early when that fails. For an MLD client that lookup can
never succeed: the client is in sta_table once, under its MLD address, while the
agent reports metrics per leg, keyed by the leg's own address.

So every per-link measurement was discarded on the first line of the handler,
before 99996's writer could see it.

Measured on hardware 2026-08-04, MLO client on the colocated controller:

	agent   leg ae:64:a9:d9:06:b3 on 76:04:1c:81:bc:2e   rssi -43
	        leg 4e:0f:4f:00:d6:5f on 7a:04:1c:81:9c:2e   rssi 0
	        leg b6:f6:c2:8f:c2:65 on 7e:04:1c:81:7c:2e   rssi 0

	sta     7a:6f:6d:db:82:92 only - the MLD address, no legs
	log     No STA found in Assoc-Link-Metrics-Resp        5x
	db      affiliated_sta.rcpi = 0 on all three legs

The agent measures the right leg and reports it correctly. Nothing was wrong
with the measurement, the emission, the persistence or the writer 99996 added -
the report simply died on a lookup that cannot succeed for the entity being
reported.

Walk the BSS entries whether or not a struct sta was found, hand every entry to
the affiliated element, and keep the struct sta updates behind a null check.
The zeros on the idle legs are honest and are handled by the same rule as
everywhere else: an unmeasured value does not overwrite a measured one.

Note for the record: this was predicted as an agent-side defect (the "strongest
link" fallback being unreachable). It is not - the agent had -43 on the correct
leg the whole time. The block was on this side.
--- a/src/cntlr_map.c
+++ b/src/cntlr_map.c
@@ -3016,9 +3016,21 @@
 
 		idx++;
 
+		/* A leg of an MLD client has no entry in sta_table - the client
+		 * is there once, under its MLD address - so bailing out here
+		 * threw away every per-link measurement before anything could
+		 * look at it. Measured 2026-08-04 with an MLO client on 4g:
+		 *
+		 *   agent   leg ae:64:a9:d9:06:b3 on 76:04:1c:81:bc:2e  rssi -43
+		 *   sta     only 7a:6f:6d:db:82:92 (the MLD address)
+		 *   log     "No STA found in Assoc-Link-Metrics-Resp"  5x
+		 *
+		 * The agent measures the right leg and says so; the report died
+		 * on a lookup that cannot succeed for legs. Keep walking the BSS
+		 * entries even without a struct sta, and let the affiliated
+		 * element take the reading.
+		 */
 		s = cntlr_find_sta(c->sta_table, p->macaddr);
-		if (!s)
-			continue;
 
 		offset = sizeof(*p);
 		for (i = 0; i < p->num_bss; i++) {
@@ -3032,6 +3044,19 @@
 				continue;
 			}
 
+#if (EASYMESH_VERSION >= 6)
+			/* Independent of sta_table: this is keyed by the leg. */
+			cntlr_affiliated_sta_metrics(c, p->macaddr, b->bssid,
+						     b->ul_rcpi,
+						     BUF_GET_BE32(b->dl_thput),
+						     BUF_GET_BE32(b->ul_thput));
+#endif
+
+			if (!s) {
+				offset += sizeof(*b);
+				continue;
+			}
+
 			if (memcmp(s->bssid, b->bssid, 6)) {
 				cntlr_dbg(LOG_STA,
 					  "%s: Ignore STA " MACFMT " link-metrics with different bssid\n",
@@ -3053,22 +3078,10 @@
 			else if (!s->de_sta->rcpi)
 				s->de_sta->rcpi = b->ul_rcpi;
 
-#if (EASYMESH_VERSION >= 6)
-			/* For a leg of an MLD client this is a per-link
-			 * measurement, and the row that gets persisted is the
-			 * affiliated element, not this struct sta. Nothing
-			 * copied between the two, so affiliated_sta.rcpi stayed
-			 * NULL however well the agent measured. */
-			cntlr_affiliated_sta_metrics(c, p->macaddr, b->bssid,
-						     b->ul_rcpi,
-						     BUF_GET_BE32(b->dl_thput),
-						     BUF_GET_BE32(b->ul_thput));
-#endif
-
 			offset += sizeof(*b);
 		}
 
-		if (iidx < INFORM_STA_MAXNUM - 1)
+		if (s && iidx < INFORM_STA_MAXNUM - 1)
 			memcpy(&inform_stalist[6 * iidx++], s->de_sta->macaddr, 6);
 	}
 
